AnimalMagic <AnimalMagic@petersbackyard.org> wrote:
>
>  Can the DOS executable be compiled from within Linux?

This is no officially supported way of building NetHack.

The main problem is that the build process generates binaries that
must be run on the target platform to generate code from the data
files.

You could cross-compile some of the binaries from the util directory
and then run the binaries in an emulator (I had to do this partly for
my AROS port) but it's tedious and error prone.

If you really mean DOS executables and not Windows binaries that run
in the command prompt I would recommend using VirtualBox or maybe
DOSBox to setup a MS-DOS environment to compile NetHack.

